{"availability":"available","full":"alimardon123/pondra","name":"pondra","description":"Pondra is one Rust binary that is a streaming store, a lakehouse and a SQL engine at once. Object storage (a local directory, S3, R2, MinIO) holds all the state: there is no Postgres, no ZooKeeper, no Kafka, no JVM.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T11:20:26Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:16:33Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alimardon123.github.io/pondra/","topics":[],"demo":"https://alimardon123.github.io/pondra/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.258Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.258Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.258Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.258Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Documentation: alimardon123.github.io/pondra — how to install it, load and query data, stream, run a cluster, and every statement, function, flag and endpoint, each example tested.","One Rust binary (55,000 lines) that ingests streams, stores them as a lakehouse (Parquet files plus a catalog, on object storage; Delta Lake and Iceberg metadata for other engines on request), keeps SQL views and streaming state up to date, answers SQL, and scales out by starting more copies of itself on the same bucket. It reads and writes what is outside it too: files on any store, other engines' Delta and Iceberg tables, Kafka clusters. Object storage is the only state: no Postgres, no ZooKeeper, no Kafka, no JVM. Runs on a local directory, any S3-compatible store (S3, Cloudflare R2,…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alimardon123/pondra/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6bacd3e8ee7eb7480946c599cf1b61b1640f91b4c99982355e7869bac33f2149","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.342Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.342Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Documentati